think Wrote the third and final onboarding video-script: "How to Contribute" — a ~3:30 walkthrough that turns a newcomer who can build and prove a module into one who writes one the Grain way and sends it back.
think Structure: TAME in one breath (safety first, performance second, joy third — bounded, asserted, explicit widths); the shape of a module (the opening triad, an assert with a why-comment); prove-before-you-claim (the witness, green before the claim); the send (a short prefixed subject, a plain honest body, docs in step, signed work — green before send); and the flow (fork, build, prove green, send). The closing frames the discipline as care, never gatekeeping.
obs The disciplines are summarized in the project's own words for a watchable form — no doc reproduced verbatim, identity-clean, generic second person, ships in the seed. It completes the series: What Is Grain (why), Build a Module (the loop), How to Contribute (the way).
obs Reach, not new capability. The season's modules are all built and the seed is live; these three scripts are the public-facing onramp — text a tool turns into video, no account or render step from the agent.
file manual/video-scripts/contributing-walkthrough.md the third video script, completing the onboarding trilogy
recommend keep-going the onboarding video trilogy is complete and ships in the seed; reaches the live repo on the next publish. A fresh module or a new surface is the next natural build whenever Keaton names one